# Applied on top of Apple Containerization's arm64 guest config and
# needy.config, for the `vz` actor runtime (Virtualization.framework on Apple
# silicon).
# Base: `containerization-arm64.config` is a byte-for-byte copy of
# Containerization 0.54.0's arm64 kernel config, which that project builds
# for Virtualization.framework guests (virtio over PCI, GICv3, PSCI, `hvc0`):
# Source: https://github.com/apple/containerization/blob/baf212e5a8e432e539beee325050aa26443a154d/kernel/config-arm64
# Reference: https://github.com/apple/containerization/blob/baf212e5a8e432e539beee325050aa26443a154d/kernel/README.md
# (Apache-2.0. Its header says Linux 6.1.68; Containerization's own Makefile
# builds it for 6.18.5 with `olddefconfig`,
# https://github.com/apple/containerization/blob/baf212e5a8e432e539beee325050aa26443a154d/kernel/Makefile#L15.)
# In that base, VIRTIO_PCI (L3044), VIRTIO_BLK (L1822), VIRTIO_CONSOLE
# (L2135), VIRTIO_VSOCKETS (L1531), FUSE_FS (L3369), TIME_NS (L187) and
# BINFMT_MISC (L857) are already `y`; HWMON is off (L2377), and needy.config
# turns it on for fake_coretemp. These lines only pin what the `vz` runtime
# depends on: the rootfs on virtio-blk, the console on `hvc0`.
CONFIG_VIRTIO_PCI=y
CONFIG_VIRTIO_BLK=y
CONFIG_VIRTIO_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_HVC_DRIVER=y
CONFIG_EXT4_FS=y
